    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰγι-κορεῖς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έων</span>,
			οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>goatherds</i>; name of one of the four Ionic tribes in
			Attica (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.66
			</span></i>, who makes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰγικόρης</span> son
			of Ion), <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i><i>lon</i><i><span class="en">
				1581
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; also at Cyzicus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.144
			</span></i>, cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰγικορὶς</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ath.Mitt.</u>
					9.27
				</span></i>
			. (Expl. as <i>goatherds</i>, but this is doubtful.)</div>
